JETCARP is dual-licensed under the Unlicense and the MIT licence.

You may use JETCARP's own code and data under either licence, at your option:

  * UNLICENSE   - a public-domain dedication (https://unlicense.org)
  * LICENSE-MIT - the MIT licence, for places that do not recognise a
                  public-domain dedication

The aim is public-domain research software. The MIT licence is offered only
as a fallback.

A few files contain or are derived from other people's work and keep their
own licences. Those licences are compatible with this dual licence, but their
notices must be kept. The files and their licences are listed in
THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md. Compiled releases also include the notices of the
Rust libraries that JETCARP is built with.
